check - check a mounted volume and repair it

  check /home
  check -n /home

Compares each file's directory record with its cluster chain in the
allocation table. A power cut mid-write can leave them inconsistent.

Repairs:
  lost clusters (marked used, reached by no file) are freed
  chains longer than the file size are trimmed
  sizes larger than the chain are corrected
  chains that leave the volume or loop are ended at the last valid cluster
  differing FAT copies are resynchronised from the first

Cross-linked clusters (claimed by two files) are reported, not repaired.
The volume is then mounted read-only.

-n reports without changing anything.

A volume not unmounted cleanly is checked automatically at mount. Nothing
on the volume may be open while check runs.
